  "mechanism": [
    "Real Exec AllocMem(MEMF_CHIP) chooses the owner. Native region and typed runtime-equate extents supply exclusions; they are not guessed address-looking words.",
    "Staged input, image, display and diagnostic backing are acquired before CMD_READ. A rejected owner is freed; one real scratch lease quarantines the collided range before retry. An unexpected scratch base or second collision fails closed.",
    "The native canonical planner validates the actual returned base before GO. Only explicit runtime-only LONG-data source coordinates are patched by the guest; the whole staged payload and copied prefix are checked with the exact admitted fixup.",
    "Guest loader code is read back against its assembled bytes. The owner and scratch leases remain live through gameplay and the post-ending observation.",
    "Pre-entry faults release dynamic leases and static backing. An acknowledged final phase frees telemetry and mailbox too; completion is observed at the exact verified assembly label, including possible ROM-task preemption. No OS return is claimed by that diagnostic hold."
  ],
